{"version":"0.12.23","prev_tag":"v0.12.22","target":"default","tag_prefix":"","area_scope":[],"commits":[{"sha":"c3ecda8d4583560422b558df78fa61f5004027aa","title":"build(deps-dev): bump ruff from 0.16.3 to 0.16.4 in the python group (#1244)","files":["uv.lock"]},{"sha":"90a232aaff12d9a2fa21fc9fe43a5c6a20074ddf","title":"Keep Task agent choices and make stalled work visible (#1301)","files":["TESTING.md","docs/architecture-reference.md","docs/authoring.md","docs/concept-review.md","docs/lf.md","performance/budgets.json","python/tests/test_gate_bounded.py","python/tests/test_resource_envelope.py","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/task/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/durable.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/loopflow.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/flow/build.yaml","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/flow/pursue.yaml","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/flow/ship-demo.yaml","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/flow/ship.yaml","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/flow/slice.yaml","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/flow/task-gate.yaml","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/compress.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/concept-review.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/implement.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/launch-plan.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/loop-decide.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/review-slice.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow_graph.rs","rust/loopflow/src/harness/claude.rs","rust/loopflow/src/harness/codex.rs","rust/loopflow/src/harness/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/harness/opencode.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/list.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/waves.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lib.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/chapter_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/flow_session.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/human_session.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/linear_observe.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pr.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_execution.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/run_record.rs","rust/loopflow/src/run_record/activity.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/children.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations/drafts/task_agent__68a92ff62c982aa17c4525170cbd3f4a.sql","rust/loopflow/src/store/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/children.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/durable.rs","rust/loopflow/src/work/task/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/flow_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/pr_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/status_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/support/ambient.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/support/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/task_initialization_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/wave_repository_ownership.rs","scripts/resource_envelope.py","scripts/test.py","swift/Loopflow/Models/TaskFlow.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Design/WorkspaceStyle.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/TaskFlowView.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/WorkSurfaceView.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/WorkspaceNavigator.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/TaskFlowProofTests.swift","tests/fixtures/dto/README.md","tests/fixtures/dto/task_execution_stalled.json","tests/fixtures/dto/task_flow_stalled.json","tests/goldens/builtin_implement.md","tests/goldens/builtin_review_slice.md","wave/infrastructure/MEMORY.md"]},{"sha":"513966f4ad7c258dcdf6f8a3b0d3fb9eecd49f24","title":"Delete Linear Tasks through lf and consolidate planning commands (#1302)","files":["README.md","TESTING.md","docs/agent-api.md","docs/architecture-reference.md","docs/architecture/homes.md","docs/architecture/planning.md","docs/authoring.md","docs/conducting.md","docs/config.md","docs/getting-started.md","docs/lf.md","docs/troubleshooting.md","docs/waves.md","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/task/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/README.md","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/relocate.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/init.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/loopflow.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/start-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/advance.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/design.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/launch-plan.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/task_pursue.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/mutate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/scan.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/split-wave.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/update-wave.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave_operate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave_start-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/config.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/git.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/prompt.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/skills.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/worktrees.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/placement.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/runs.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/ssh.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/top.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/util.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/waves.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/work.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/chapter.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/chapter_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/child.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/error.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/human_session.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/land.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/linear_observe.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm/oauth_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm/task_comments_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm/task_planning_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm/test_fixture.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pr.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/project.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_pm.rs","rust/loopflow/src/pm/linear.rs","rust/loopflow/src/pm/linear/deletion_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/run_record.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/chapters.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/children.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations/drafts/task_deletions__1b2d47152bceed3f3251bc97a26cb01d.sql","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations/drafts/task_issue_identities__01517af294fcda7f536be29e4709530b.sql","rust/loopflow/src/store/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/chapters.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/children.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/durable.rs","rust/loopflow/src/work/chapter.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/dto_fixtures.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/flow_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/pr_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/repository_team_matrix.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/session_cli_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/status_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/task_deletion_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/task_github_cache_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/task_initialization_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/wave_repository_ownership.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/wave_resolution_matrix.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/wave_resolution_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/worktree_tests.rs","skills/loopflow/SKILL.md","swift/Loopflow/Models/TaskComments.swift","swift/Loopflow/Services/RegistryQuery.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/MacLocalWaveAgentLauncher.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/DTOFixtureTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/LocalWaveAgentLauncherTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/RegistryQueryTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/TaskCommentsProofTests.swift"]},{"sha":"841164083e87779158b572ccc908a8d4f0dfab6a","title":"Let a release retry its version after a withdrawn PR, and bound the Swift test step (#1305)","files":[".github/workflows/ci.yml","rust/loopflow/src/ops/release.rs"]}],"merged_prs":[{"number":1244,"title":"build(deps-dev): bump ruff from 0.16.3 to 0.16.4 in the python group","body":"Bumps the python group with 1 update: [ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff).\n\nUpdates `ruff` from 0.16.3 to 0.16.4\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/releases\">ruff's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.16.4</h2>\n<h2>Release Notes</h2>\n<p>Released on 2026-08-20.</p>\n<h3>Preview features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[<code>flake8-use-pathlib</code>] Add autofix for <code>PTH116</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/26460\">#26460</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>refurb</code>] Restrict <code>delete-full-slice</code> to lists (<code>FURB131</code>) (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27711\">#27711</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>refurb</code>] Skip <code>FURB101</code> and <code>FURB103</code> when the <code>open</code> argument is a file descriptor (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27643\">#27643</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix <code>InvalidInstruction</code> on Windows CPUs that do not support <code>POPCNT</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27803\">#27803</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>pyflakes</code>] Emit semantic syntax errors in string type definitions as <code>F722</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27835\">#27835</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>pylint</code>] Allow <code>os._exit</code> imports in <code>import-private-name</code> (<code>PLC2701</code>) (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27738\">#27738</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Rule changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[syntax-errors] Align mixed t-string/bytes error message with CPython 3.14 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27766\">#27766</a>)</li>\n<li>[<code>ruff</code>] Add <code>ctypes.LittleEndianStructure</code> and related types to existing exception (<code>RUF012</code>) (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27753\">#27753</a>)</li>\n<li>[syntax-errors] Detect duplicate keyword arguments (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/17804\">#17804</a>)</li>\n<li>[syntax-errors] Detect parameters declared <code>nonlocal</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27628\">#27628</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Server</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Offer display-only fixes and mark safe fixes preferred (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27807\">#27807</a>)</li>\n<li>Support pull diagnostics for notebook cells (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27779\">#27779</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add default indicator to rules table (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27724\">#27724</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix broken link to Python docs (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27757\">#27757</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Other changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix s390x stacker assembly in release builds (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27776\">#27776</a>)</li>\n<li>Guarantee minimum stack size when parsing a module, standalone expression, and suites (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/25464\">#25464</a>)</li>\n<li>Reduce configuration deserialization code size (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27924\">#27924</a>)</li>\n<li>Check packed AST index bounds (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27849\">#27849</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Contributors</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/AbhinavMir\"><code>@​AbhinavMir</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eduardorittner\"><code>@​eduardorittner</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/royb3\"><code>@​royb3</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/MichaReiser\"><code>@​MichaReiser</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/carljm\"><code>@​carljm</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rosstitmarsh\"><code>@​rosstitmarsh</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/ntBre\"><code>@​ntBre</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>So","files":[],"additions":69,"deletions":69,"changed_files":1,"merge_commit":"c3ecda8d4583560422b558df78fa61f5004027aa"},{"number":1301,"title":"Keep Task agent choices and make stalled work visible","body":"Unattended Tasks could ignore `-m` and leave failed decisions looking ready. This change persists the Task's agent choice, exposes blocked and stalled execution, and shortens the implementation loop.\n\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [Make the default Task Flow converge, and let a Task choose its agent · LOO-319](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-319/make-the-default-task-flow-converge-and-let-a-task-choose-its-agent)\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## What changes\n\n- Task choice overrides skill defaults through launch, resume, restart and review; the configured default stays unchanged.\n- Failed decisions retain their Run and open a keyed unblock Session. CLI and desktop share the blocked/stalled state and recovery guidance.\n- Five minutes without events or sampled body/tool CPU progress shows Stalled. Missing or mismatched samples stay Unknown; observation grants no termination authority.\n- Pursue becomes implement → compress → review-slice → loop-decide. Compress edits code, review-slice reports replacement evidence and convergence blockers, and concept-review stays interactive. Shipping drops the redundant task-gate wrapper.\n- Only free disk gates builds. Oversized siblings warn; the current checkout cleans its own oversized disposable build roots.\n\n## Checks\n\nFinal materialized Rust suite: 2,062 passed, eight skipped. The affected gate also passed 244 Python tests, 338 Swift tests, 78 website tests, the app build and eight Wave fixture renders. Formatting, Clippy, Ruff, architecture and migration checks passed. Gate failures in fixture isolation, catalog output, decision positions and retained-Run expectations were reproduced and repaired without changing production behavior.\n\nConfigured Claude launch/resume, a live five-minute stall, rendered Task states and live proof of the final decision-policy revision remain unverified. Earlier Codex policy proof used simulated PM and synthetic feedback. The non-Rust results precede only test-fixture and evidence-note edits; no hosted CI result is claimed. [Decisions and proof limits](https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/blob/cbf50592dbef59660bbc1df6617ea92bfa5bd05e/wave/infrastructure/MEMORY.md#task-convergence-loo-319-branch-evidence-2026-09-27) remain preserved for delivery.","files":[],"additions":3105,"deletions":964,"changed_files":75,"merge_commit":"90a232aaff12d9a2fa21fc9fe43a5c6a20074ddf"},{"number":1302,"title":"Delete Linear Tasks through lf and consolidate planning commands","body":"Removing a Task previously required separate Linear and local actions, while planning commands were split across `task`, `pm`, and `work`. This PR adds retryable Task deletion and groups planning operations under Task, Wave, and repository commands.\n\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [Cancel Linear issues through lf: pm task cancel, and abandon cancels its issue · LOO-305](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-305/cancel-linear-issues-through-lf-pm-task-cancel-and-abandon-cancels-its)\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## What changes\n\n- Add `lf task delete ISSUE` for registered and planning-only Tasks. Confirmed deletion removes them from current planning views while preserving completed outcomes, timestamps, authored files, and retained PRs.\n- Persist issue identity and deletion confirmation so retries survive planning refresh and chapter replacement. Missing provider data never counts as confirmation. Chapter rotation now deletes untouched backlog through Linear’s native trash operation.\n- Consolidate Task creation, editing, comments, and completion under `lf task`. Planning-only creation needs no checkout or execution credentials; `create --run` validates execution before filing and reuses the issue on retry.\n- Move connection, sync, and placement to `lf wave`, provider administration to `lf repo`, and planning diagnostics to `lf doctor --planning`. Remove `pm`/`work` and superseded Task commands without aliases; update desktop callers, skills, and documentation.\n- Resolve checkout Task identity from its checked-out branch, and preserve completion evidence across provider writeback retries.\n\nDeletion does not certify process termination or complete Session/Run cleanup. Recorded Runs retain their attribution, and explicit `lf task status ISSUE` preserves historical lookup.\n\n## Checks\n\nAdded coverage for deletion confirmation, lost responses, retained history, creation/completion retries, migrations, and chapter rotation. A Linux-only CLI integration test exercises synthetic Linear state in an isolated Home; planning fixtures now pin their executable so merge reconciliation needs no installed `lf`.\n\nChecks were not rerun for this description. [Recorded branch evidence](wave/infrastructure/MEMORY.md) reports focused checks and Clippy passing, but no full gate or installed acceptance.\n\n## Try it\n\nSuggested walkthrough, not performed for this description: in a disposable development Home connected to a test Wave, create a planning Task with `lf task create --wave <wave> --title \"Deletion walkthrough\"`. Delete its returned identifier with `lf task delete ISSUE`, then repeat the deletion. After `lf wave sync --wave <wave>`, the Task should be absent from current planning, and the repeated deletion should succeed.","files":[],"additions":7242,"deletions":3054,"changed_files":113,"merge_commit":"513966f4ad7c258dcdf6f8a3b0d3fb9eecd49f24"},{"number":1305,"title":"Let a release retry its version after a withdrawn PR, and bound the Swift test step","body":"Two fixes that were blocking the v0.12.23 release on 2026-09-27.\n\n**`lf release run` starts fresh after a withdrawn release PR.** A release PR closed without merging stays attached to its branch name on GitHub. The next run for that version found it and stopped with advice to rename the release branch, which the version-derived name does not allow. The only way forward was to skip the version. The lookup now returns the version's open or merged PR and ignores withdrawn ones.\n\n**The Swift test step has a 20 minute limit.** It hangs intermittently in an observation cancellation test and had no limit. On 2026-09-27 it held a release PR for over four hours and main for ninety minutes. A hang now fails and can be rerun. The hang itself is not fixed here.\n\nChecks: 41 of 41 tests in the release module, including a new one for the lookup; Clippy clean. The release path was not exercised end to end; the next release run is that proof.","files":[],"additions":36,"deletions":11,"changed_files":2,"merge_commit":"841164083e87779158b572ccc908a8d4f0dfab6a"}],"decisions":null,"previous_release_notes":"# v0.12.22\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.22 keeps a Task's plan, conversation, review feedback, and running work together. The Mac app brings them into one workspace, while saved Flows carry work through revision and blocked PR landings can recover on the same commit. Getting started also requires less configuration: unconfigured runs choose an installed coding agent, and display names can come from Git.\n\n## Follow a Task without losing your place\n\nThe Mac app now uses one repository → Wave → Task → Session outline. Selecting a Task exposes its Flow, comments, and running work; entering a Session retains the surrounding workspace.\n\n- Choose Compact, Full hierarchy, or Sessions presentations. Started Tasks appear before they have a Session, unattributed conversations remain under **Orphan sessions**, and navigation state survives repository switches.\n- Preview a Task's Flow before **Start**. Once started, inspect its captured definition, current step, and loop iteration, then **Resume** or use the confirmed **Stop & restart…** action.\n- Read recent Runs and Linear comments from the Task overview. Failed comment reads retain the earlier thread with **May be out of date** and **Retry**.\n- Open **Monitor** beside Sessions and shells to follow active Task Runs. Incomplete observations remain visible rather than being reported as confirmed emptiness.\n- Switching to a Session in another checkout restores its conversation, companion terminals, split layout, and focus. **New conversation** opens a scoped prompt without creating a Task or starting its Flow.\n- Rename Sessions in place or with `lf session rename <id> \"Name\"`. Agent suggestions preserve names chosen by a person.\n\n## Continue from review to the next useful step\n\n`lf task advance <issue>` drives a Task's saved Flow until input, a blocker, interruption, or completion. Recovery retains captured definitions, selected branches, and completed review feedback, so revision does not require reconstructing the work.\n\n- The `feature` Flow connects design review to implementation, compression, behavioral and concept reviews, explicit loop decisions, and an interactive demo. Demo feedback can lead to another implementation pass.\n- **Complete** replaces Approve/Iterate in CLI and desktop Sessions. Completing the Session returns feedback; the following decision step chooses where the Flow goes next.\n- Blocked decisions reuse one Ask and reassess its answer. Decisions take effect only after their originating Run succeeds, and stale workers cannot settle newer work.\n- Ordinary Flows are resumable too. Finishing a Flow does not implicitly merge its PR or complete its Task.\n- Launching inside a Task's worktree without an explicit Work selector now associates the launch with that Task. `lf --task ID` accepts direct Flows and inline prompts as well as skills.\n\n## Recover delivery without an empty commit\n\nAfter resolving an external blocker, rerun `lf pr land` on the same head. Landing reconciles fresh GitHub evidence after repairs and reports the repair agent's concrete conclusion.\n\n- Blocked landings can resume without a lifetime repair ceiling or a required SHA change. GitHub's confirmed merge takes precedence over provider errors.\n- Repair publication preserves active checkout placement and the intended Task disposition, including `-c` or `--next <slug>`.\n- Rebase recreates deleted remote branches despite stale tracking refs, while leases continue protecting unseen remote work.\n- Preparing a replacement PR head explicitly removes the PR from GitHub's merge queue before publication.\n\n## See what happened during Wave operation\n\nEach Wave wake runs one `wave/operate` attempt, with failures, input claims, and provider sessions recorded in the turn journal. This simplifies Wave operation while Tasks and ordinary Flows retain their execution engines.\n\n- Wave stack traversal, queue/skip controls, and playhead state are removed. A later unrelated successful wake cannot erase an earlier recorded failure.\n- `lf wave recover <name>` displays the original historical continuation. Canceling it requires its exact source sequence and a reason; unknown provider liveness blocks replacement.\n- `lf runs --active [--task ID] [--json]` reports current provider-backed Runs and observation gaps. macOS also supports streaming snapshots with `--watch --json`; Linux supports one-shot reads.\n- Desktop Task terminals use Ghostty with a pool owned by each workspace. The tmux plugin and desktop tmux shells are removed; timer rendering handles unavailable display links.\n\n## Start with the agent and name already configured\n\nThe first-run guidance now explains the plan–build–review workflow and leads with the Mac app. Agent selection and naming use existing local configuration, while request authors remain attached to their original requests.\n\n- Unconfigured runs select the first installed agent in order: Codex, Claude Code, OpenCode. Explicit configuration and skill defaults retain precedence; missing-agent errors include installation guidance.\n- The Mac app explains how to recover when opening a non-Git folder. Documentation adds a glossary, prerequisites, and provider-cost guidance; Task delivery still requires Git, Linear, and GitHub setup.\n- Inspect the resolved display name with `lf user name --json`, replacing `lf name`. A personal Loopflow override takes precedence over Git's `user.name`, including repository overrides.\n- Reopening or moving a Session resumes its conversation without injecting a participant-update prompt. A missing Loopflow name preference no longer tells the agent to disregard a familiar name.\n- Request authors survive CLI and Mac chat, journal replay, Discord, and Linear without being reassigned to publishers or editors. Unknown authors remain unknown, and display names do not establish authorization.\n\n## Operational notes\n\n- Existing Flow invocations retain their captured definitions. Start a fresh invocation to replace obsolete review navigation policies. Inspect interrupted external operations before retrying them.\n- Wave listeners and residents must use matching binaries. Historical queues are not automatically transferred into ordinary Flows. Unclosed attempts still require authoritative termination reconciliation; this release does not add that command.\n- Minor releases share a product snapshot with their closing patch: publish a new patch when changes remain, otherwise reuse the latest completed patch. Patch notes cover the preceding release; minor notes cover the cycle since the preceding `.0` tag. Persisted pair selection supports retries, but recovery receipts remain local to the controller.\n- `lf release notes VERSION --preview` generates notes without changing release archives or manifests. Existing versions use their historical tag and context. Minor publication stops before tagging if the merged candidate differs from the prepared snapshot.\n- The Mac workspace currently supports light mode only. The `design` and `ship-5whys` single-step Flow wrappers are removed; invoke them as skills. Bare names prefer skills, with `lf skill <name>` and `lf flow <name>` available for explicit selection.\n- Recorded recovery and publication checks include simulated provider/GitHub boundaries; live branch recreation and configured release-note previews were observed. Live provider continuation, hosted recovery, and hosted UI acceptance remain unverified in the supplied evidence. The recorded default local gate had a Flow Session fixture conflict between `LF_HOME` and `LF_CONTROL_HOME`; its broad Rust pass used an isolated Home without that pin.\n\n## Small changes\n\n- Specialized operating instructions live in the skills that use them, reducing universal prompt guidance. Durable lessons live in Wave memory; retired directions and orphaned attribution notes are removed, while chapter archives remain in `.lf/chapters/`.\n- `lf ls --current` excludes abandoned and retired registrations. `lf work forget wave <id>` removes an empty abandoned registration and supports `--dry-run`.\n- Development Session reopen commands retain the development executable. Stored Codex OAuth no longer overrides native login.\n- Terminal test polling reads fresh state before evaluating its deadline.\n- Seven Rust dependencies are updated, and the repository includes the MIT license.","source_limits":{"context_bytes":131072,"commits":256,"merged_prs":200,"files_per_change":100,"area_scopes":32,"name_bytes":256,"title_bytes":300,"path_bytes":512,"pr_body_bytes":4096,"decisions_bytes":16384,"previous_release_notes_bytes":16384,"release_notes_bytes":61440},"omissions":{"commits":0,"merged_prs":0,"commit_files":13,"pr_files":0,"area_scopes":0,"text_bytes":8677,"decisions_bytes":0,"previous_release_notes_bytes":0}}